<attributes_schema>
{{attributes_schema}}
</attributes_schema>

<category>
{{category}}
</category>

<subcategory>
{{subcategory}}
</subcategory>

<product_data>
<title>
{{product.title}}
</title>

<description>
{{product.description}}
</description>
{% if product.metadata is not none %}

<metadata>
{{ product.metadata }}
</metadata>
{% endif %}
</product_data>

Extract the attributes listed in <attributes_schema> for the product in <product_data>. The product belongs to the category and subcategory above.

For each attribute in the schema:
- If the title, description or metadata states the attribute, or its value can be determined from them, give that value. When the schema lists possible values for the attribute, use the listed value that matches best. For colors, use the closest listed color.
- Otherwise, set the value to null. The results fill a product catalog, so an empty value is better than a guessed one.

Include every attribute in the schema, even when its value is null.
